SUMMARY:Love\, Simon (2018): Laugh Out Loud Pride Film Screening NEW
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a FREE family friendly screening the 2019 GLAAD Media Award Winner\, “Love\, Simon\,” to wrap up Pride this year at Montclair Public Library! The screening will be followed by a open panel discussion about the film featuring queer film makers Mac Allen\, Erby Beauvil and FDU Professor Cordelia Siporin. Free popcorn will be provided by The Claridge. These screenings are proudly co-presented by Pride Center of Montclair. Come join in the fun and bring a friend! \n“Seventeen-year-old Simon keeps a huge secret from his family\, his friends and all of his classmates: he’s gay. When that secret is threatened by a blackmailer\, Simon must come to terms with his identity.” Rated TV-14 \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/love-simon-2018-laugh-out-loud-pride-film-screening-new/
LOCATION:Montclair Public Library\, 50 South Fullerton Avenue\, Montclair\, New Jersey\, 07042\, United States
CATEGORIES:Comedy,Community,Entertainment,Film
